WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.160
Have you ever wondered

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:06.080
if there are more natural ways
to lower your high blood pressure,

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.040
guard against Alzheimer's,
lose weight, and feel better?

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.240
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.720
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.320
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.200
Today, we look at the
best ways to treat ADHD,

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.520
and we start by taking a close look
at the effects of artificial food colors

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.520
in children’s diets.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.680
Nearly 50 years ago,

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:33.040
Cedars-Sinai Chief of Pediatrics
Ben Feingold,

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.120
published heresy,

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.120
suggesting that
artificial food colors

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.320
could induce
behavioral disturbances.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.080
Dow Chemical disagreed,
as did Coca Cola,

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.120
as well as other players

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.160
within the trillion-dollar
processed food industry,

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.640
who were able to convince
the medical establishment

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.480
that it was all just one
elaborate placebo effect.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.680
But the truth can only be buried
so long.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.680
In 2004,
a randomized, double-blind,

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.320
placebo-controlled
food challenge was published.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:06.400
Hyperactivity in preschoolers
was significantly reduced

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.840
when artificial colorings

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.000
and the preservative
sodium benzoate

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.240
were eliminated
from their diets;

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.160
but hyperactivity
jumped back up

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.320
when the additives,
rather than a placebo,

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.520
were reintroduced
into their diets.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.760
The researchers suggest
the benefit would accrue

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.000
for all children
if they didn't consume

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.080
artificial food colors
or benzoate preservatives.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:29.920
Then another randomized,
double-blind,

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:31.920
placebo-controlled
food challenge was published

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:35.360
in probably the most prestigious
medical journal in the world.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.520
This time, researchers found
that artificial colors

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.280
and other food additives
in processed foods

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.800
appeared to exacerbate
hyperactive behaviors;

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.120
impulsivity, inattentiveness,
and overactivity,

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.640
among young children,

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:48.880
with more pronounced effects
in 3-year-olds

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:50.720
relative to 8-or 9-year-olds.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:53.120
And indeed, a more recent
randomized controlled trial

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:55.280
in 8- or 9-year-olds
in Hong Kong

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.680
didn't observe
a significant effect.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.200
The authors suggested
it may be

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.840
because older kids
may be less sensitive,

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:04.240
or the dose used
was too small

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:07.120
relative to what
the kids typically consumed.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.400
But what happens in children
already diagnosed with ADHD

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.880
if you remove
artificial food colors?

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:15.200
In a meta-analysis
of randomized controlled trials

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.920
for dietary interventions
for ADHD,

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:20.800
excluding artificial food colors
from the diet

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.840
significantly improved behavior.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.280
In this meta-analysis,

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.400
the data over here suggest
that food colors were harmful,

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.080
whether assessed by parents,
observers,

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.440
or attention tests,

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.400
compared to studies
showing the opposite.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.560
You can actually see
the difference in brain waves

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:39.280
on EEG compared to placebo.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.120
As I highlighted years ago,

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.080
the European Union
requires warning labels

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.720
of potential adverse effects
on activity and attention

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:47.840
in children.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.000
However, although
the Food and Drug Administration

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.040
in the United States has banned
a few artificial colors

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.600
like Red Dye No.1,
Red Dye No. 2,

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:59.200
Red Dye No. 4
due to cancer concerns,

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.720
no warning labels are required,

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.160
and many artificial colors

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.880
still predominate
processed foods.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:07.760
Among grocery store products
marketed to children,

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:12.720
about 40 percent contain
at least one artificial color.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:13.520
In 2021,

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:17.600
a report from the California
Environmental Protection Agency

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.560
highlighted the potential
neurobehavioral effects

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:22.800
of artificial food dyes
in children.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:23.760
The authors concluded

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.640
that although not all studies
implicated them,

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.080
the current medical literature

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.400
provides a substantial amount
of evidence

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.880
that consumption
of synthetic food dyes

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:36.480
is associated with adverse
neurobehavioral outcomes

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.520
in kids,

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:40.240
and the FDA's
Acceptable Daily Intake levels

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:43.360
may not adequately
protect children.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.560
For years I've been concerned
that Red No. 3

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.560
still hasn't been banned
from food,

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.960
given that it was banned
more than 30 years ago

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.760
from inclusion in any products
that go on our skin

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.200
due to cancer risk.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.440
Finally, in October 2023,

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:59.920
the California Food Safety Act
was signed,

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.480
banning Red Dye No. 3
from foods and drinks

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.240
sold throughout the state,

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:05.360
while consumer groups,

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.920
including the Center for Science
in the Public Interest,

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.880
continue to petition the FDA
for a national ban

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:13.920
to prohibit use
of this carcinogen.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.680
And on January 15 2025,

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:20.320
35 years after it was
banned in cosmetics,

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:25.920
the FDA finally banned it
nationwide in food as of 2027

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:28.960
and in drugs as of 2028.

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:29.840
In our next story,

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:33.760
the benefits of exercise in
controlling ADHD symptoms.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:38.720
Every year in the United States doctors
write 20 million prescriptions

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:41.200
for stimulants like
Ritalin to give to kids

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.840
for attention deficit
hyperactivity disorder,

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:46.240
and it goes up every year.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.000
In fact, more than
any other drug class

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.760
another 0.8 million added every
year to that 20 million.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:55.760
That's a lot of amphetamines
for a lot of kids.

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:57.200
These drugs are
thought to act by

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:00.160
increasing dopamine and norepinephrine
levels in the brain.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:03.920
Guess what else can increase
dopamine and norepinephrine levels?

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:04.720
Exercise!

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:08.560
And it happens within minutes
of getting on a bike,

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.320
levels shoot up.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.240
Medications take
an hour to work;

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.240
physical activity works
almost immediately.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:18.800
But does it work for ADHD?

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:20.720
According to the latest review,

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:23.040
-there isn't a lot of
research out there-,

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.880
but the current evidence
suggests that

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:30.320
both acute and chronic physical activity
can mitigate ADHD symptoms.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:34.960
So while "medications and exercise
with regard to ADHD"

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:38.240
"shows that they both work
to more adequately regulate"

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:41.120
"dopamine and norepinephrine
levels in the brain”,

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:44.320
some of the new long-acting
formulations of drugs

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.080
can work for up to 12 hours,

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:48.240
whereas the therapeutic
effect of exercise

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.960
may only last
an hour or so.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:53.880
But, the drugs produce
unwanted side effects

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.920
and have the potential for abuse.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.840
"Exercise has been
shown to be effective"

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:04.080
"in controlling ADHD symptoms and
has essentially no side effects".

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.160
Well, that's not really true.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:08.320
It should be noted
that a major difference

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:10.080
in the 2 treatment
modalities is that

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:13.520
medications have a defined
effect on ADHD symptoms alone,

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:17.520
whereas exercise produces
physical, mental, and emotional

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.920
advantages that
are far reaching.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:25.840
So, exercise does have side-effects,
but they're all good.

